&lt;div class=&quot;job-post-content&quot; style=&quot;position: relative; z-index: 2;&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 20px; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;max-width: 100%; float: left;&quot; src=&quot;https://i.imgur.com/b9m4CJj.jpeg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;92&quot;&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 20px; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 20px; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 20px; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;Category-defining tech. Career-defining work.&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;Lots of tech companies disrupt. But, many fail when they try to scale. We&#39;re different. CockroachDB makes it easier for companies to build and scale apps. This is how and why we&#39;re helping some of the most innovative companies on the planet. We tackle problems head-on and focus on solutions that create lasting impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;Because when our customers win, we all win.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Staff Product Marketing Manager to join our PMM team during a pivotal period of growth. This is a high-ownership role at the center of everything Cockroach Labs does: you&#39;ll own the go-to-market for a defined portfolio of product areas, serve as the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;go-to-market lead for our company rebrand&lt;/strong&gt; — the biggest brand moment in our history — and act as a launch bench across one of the densest release calendars we&#39;ve ever shipped, including major GA milestones across editions, deployment, and operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your product portfolio anchors one of our most strategic stories — how CockroachDB runs, watches, and connects itself in production: Observability &amp;amp; AI-Assisted Insights (including our new autonomous monitoring agent), Workload Management, and Ecosystem &amp;amp; Platform Integration (change data capture and how CockroachDB plugs into the modern data stack). Together these areas sit at the heart of CockroachDB&#39;s AI-operations narrative and its “fits your stack” story, and you&#39;ll shape how the market understands them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Marketing at Cockroach Labs sits inside the Product organization within R&amp;amp;D, which means you&#39;re embedded in the product development lifecycle from the start: you&#39;ll attend product planning, know the roadmap two quarters out, and author the “so what” for every feature that ships in your areas. If you like working with R&amp;amp;D in the morning, Demand Generation mid-day, and Sales in the afternoon, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You must be based in New York City to be eligible for this role, and will be expected to go into our office on Mondays, Tuesdays and Thursdays.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Positioning and messaging for your portfolio. &lt;/strong&gt;Develop, test, and deliver compelling positioning and value propositions for your product areas, tuned to the needs of key personas — developers, platform engineers, architects, and enterprise buyers. The core skill of this role is translation: taking complex technical capabilities and expressing them in language a CIO acts on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rebrand go-to-market. &lt;/strong&gt;Lead the cross-functional go-to-market program for the company rebrand: narrative, messaging migration, launch sequencing, field and customer communications, and enablement — coordinating across Product, Marketing, Sales, and Comms to land it on time and with impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product launches and releases. &lt;/strong&gt;Drive launch-grade execution for the releases in your areas and serve as a shared launch bench for marquee GA moments across the roadmap. Help install and run a standardized launch playbook used for every product release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Content and bill of materials. &lt;/strong&gt;Create high-impact collateral — product briefs, website copy, blogs, whitepapers, case studies, and sales assets — that communicates real customer value, not feature lists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales enablement. &lt;/strong&gt;Build training and enablement that Sales actually uses: where we win by vertical, use case, and persona; how to tell the cost and resilience story against Aurora, Oracle, and Spanner; and how to sell in business language rather than database terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market and competitive intelligence. &lt;/strong&gt;Analyze industry trends, customer needs, and the competitive landscape. Feed win/loss insight, product analytics, and field feedback back into positioning, roadmap conversations, and enablement priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional GTM collaboration. &lt;/strong&gt;Operate as a trusted partner to Product Management, Education, Demand Generation, and Sales. Influence outcomes across teams you don&#39;t own, and build joint deliverables that make the whole go-to-market stronger.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 30 days, &lt;/strong&gt;you&#39;ll go deep on the product (create clusters, run workloads), your journeys, and our go-to-market strategy. You&#39;ll build relationships with the PMs and engineering leaders behind your areas, audit the existing positioning and content, and get hands-on with the rebrand program plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By 60 days, &lt;/strong&gt;you&#39;ll have refined messaging for your portfolio, taken ownership of the rebrand go-to-market workstream, and built the launch plan for the next release cycle in your areas. You&#39;ll complete 200-level Cockroach University courses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By 90 days, &lt;/strong&gt;you&#39;ll be executing in full: launches shipping on your playbook, rebrand milestones on track, enablement delivered to Sales, and an operating rhythm established with Product, Demand Generation, Content, and AR/PR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of professional experience, including 5+ years in enterprise software/SaaS product marketing with a proven record of launching products to market (we&#39;re hiring at the Senior or Staff level depending on experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise infrastructure or developer-tools experience: you&#39;ve marketed deeply technical products to developers, architects, and CTOs/CIOs, and you hold your own in the room with technical buyers — ideally with exposure to the database, data infrastructure, or AI categories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional technical-to-business translation ability: you instinctively rewrite “geo-partitioned leaseholder rebalancing” as “your app is fast everywhere your customers are”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launch leadership: you&#39;ve run complex, cross-functional launches end to end — and ideally a rebrand, repositioning, or category-level messaging change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong writing chops: you produce unique, personable long-form content that technical audiences actually want to read&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical rigor: you use win/loss analysis, product analytics, and pipeline data to inform strategy, prove what&#39;s working, and kill what isn&#39;t&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thoughtfully use LLMs to radically improve PMM effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of operating cross-functionally with product, engineering, and sales as a trusted advisor — navigating ambiguity, integrating diverse perspectives, and driving measurable results without direct ownership of every outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing against cloud-native default databases (Aurora, DynamoDB, Spanner) and overcoming “good enough + already on AWS” inertia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience positioning observability, AIOps, or AI-assisted products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data integration and streaming ecosystems (change data capture, Kafka, schema registries) and how enterprises evaluate “fits my stack”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or running competitive intelligence programs (battlecards, win/loss cadences, sales feedback loops)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Head of Product Marketing, you&#39;ll join a small, high-leverage PMM team inside the broader Product organization. Product Marketing at Cockroach Labs means you work with &lt;em&gt;everyone&lt;/em&gt; — sales, sales enablement, solution engineering, product management, demand generation, and beyond. We like it that way: this team shapes the growth vector of the company every day.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
