&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 20px; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;max-width: 100%; float: left;&quot; src=&quot;https://i.imgur.com/b9m4CJj.jpeg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;92&quot;&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 20px; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 20px; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); line-height: 1.2; margin-top: 20px; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;Category-defining tech. Career-defining work.&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;Lots of tech companies disrupt. But, many fail when they try to scale. We&#39;re different. CockroachDB makes it easier for companies to build and scale apps. This is how and why we&#39;re helping some of the most innovative companies on the planet. We tackle problems head-on and focus on solutions that create lasting impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;Because when our customers win, we all win.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Staff Product Marketing Manager to own the Onboard &amp;amp; Build stage of the customer lifecycle — the moment a developer (or their agent) first meets CockroachDB and decides whether to build on it. It&#39;s the front door of our entire go-to-market motion: if we don&#39;t win here, nothing downstream matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own four connected user journeys end-to-end — Activation to Collaboration, Data Onboarding &amp;amp; Enablement, Developer Experiences, and Programmability &amp;amp; Extensibility — as a single, coherent stage rather than four disconnected pieces. That&#39;s deliberate: the developer&#39;s path from “curious” to “building in production” should feel like one story, and you&#39;re the person who makes it one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior, high-ownership role. You&#39;ll set the positioning, build the messaging, and drive the enablement and content for how developers adopt CockroachDB — including the AI-native patterns increasingly defining this stage: agent-driven discovery, MCP and agent-facing surfaces, and the reality that coding agents themselves now evaluate and choose databases. You&#39;ll sit inside Product Marketing &amp;amp; DevRel within the R&amp;amp;D organization, close to engineering and on the roadmap early enough to shape the story, not just narrate it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Below are the journeys you will own:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Activation to Collaboration. &lt;/strong&gt;The front line of the agentic strategy — how developers and their coding agents discover, evaluate, and choose CockroachDB. If an agent doesn&#39;t pick us at activation, nothing downstream happens; you own making sure we&#39;re the obvious choice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Onboarding &amp;amp; Enablement. &lt;/strong&gt;The migration and onboarding story — how teams move off legacy databases and get to production, including the AI Migration Assistant and the MOLT tooling that de-risks the path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer Experiences. &lt;/strong&gt;The end-to-end developer experience — quickstarts, docs, sample apps, and the surfaces that turn first-touch curiosity into a running application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programmability &amp;amp; Extensibility. &lt;/strong&gt;How developers extend and build on CockroachDB — the interfaces, integrations, and capabilities (SQL Server design partnerships, Dynamic SQL, and more) that make it a platform, not just a database.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Positioning &amp;amp; messaging for the stage. &lt;/strong&gt;Build the message house for Onboard &amp;amp; Build — the value propositions, proof points, and narrative that make developers choose and stay. Keep all four journeys laddering to one coherent story and to the broader company positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Launch &amp;amp; GTM execution. &lt;/strong&gt;Own the PMM deliverables for launches touching your journeys — messaging, enablement, content, and field readiness — mapped to the GTM readiness plan and shipped on time. You move fast once positioning locks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field &amp;amp; sales enablement. &lt;/strong&gt;Arm the field to sell the onboarding and developer story — first-call decks, objection handling, competitive framing, and the pitch reps carry — partnering with the enablement team on delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The AI-native adoption story. &lt;/strong&gt;Own how the agentic era shows up at this stage: agent-driven discovery, agents as a first-class audience, and the message that CockroachDB is where developers and their agents build. Turn it into proof, not just positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional partnership. &lt;/strong&gt;Work hand-in-glove with the PMs for each journey, with DevRel, docs, and demand gen — translating what&#39;s shipping into what the market hears, and bringing developer reality back into the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proof and content. &lt;/strong&gt;Drive the case studies, reference stories, and technical content that make the onboarding and build story credible — grounded in real customer outcomes, not claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 30 days, &lt;/strong&gt;you&#39;ll go deep on the product and the four journeys, meet the PMs and cross-functional partners you&#39;ll work with, and audit the existing positioning, messaging, and content across Onboard &amp;amp; Build for gaps and quick wins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By 60 days, &lt;/strong&gt;you&#39;ll have a clear point of view on where the stage&#39;s story is strong and where it&#39;s thin, shipped your first messaging or enablement deliverable, and begun driving one of the four journeys end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By 90 days, &lt;/strong&gt;you&#39;ll own the full Onboard &amp;amp; Build narrative — a coherent message house across all four journeys, active field enablement, and a working partnership with the journey PMs feeding the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8+ years in product marketing, &lt;/strong&gt;with a track record of owning positioning, messaging, and launches for technical products — ideally databases, developer tools, data infrastructure, or cloud platforms (Staff level; senior candidates with exceptional depth considered).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Genuine technical fluency. &lt;/strong&gt;You can hold a real conversation with developers and PMs about distributed systems, databases, and how software gets built — and translate it into messaging that&#39;s both accurate and compelling. You don&#39;t fake the technical depth; you have it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluency in the AI-native developer world. &lt;/strong&gt;You understand how developers build with LLMs and agents today — RAG, vector search, agent memory, MCP, agent-driven workflows — and can position data infrastructure credibly within it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A clear, opinionated point of view. &lt;/strong&gt;You bring a strong PMM perspective and defend it with evidence. You&#39;d rather challenge a weak positioning than execute it quietly, and you know how to disagree constructively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sharp technical storytelling. &lt;/strong&gt;You turn capability into meaning — “online schema changes” becomes “ship changes with zero downtime” — and you make the developer&#39;s life the center of the story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bias for decision-ready output. &lt;/strong&gt;You produce concise, high-quality work under real deadlines, flag decisions inline, and don&#39;t pad. You work fast when the direction is clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional gravity. &lt;/strong&gt;You earn trust with PMs, engineers, sales, and DevRel, and you make the story better by pulling their reality into it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Head of Product Marketing, you&#39;ll join a small, high-leverage PMM team inside the broader Product organization. Product Marketing at Cockroach Labs means you work with &lt;em&gt;everyone&lt;/em&gt; — sales, sales enablement, solution engineering, product management, demand generation, and beyond. We like it that way: this team shapes the growth vector of the company every day.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cockroach Labs is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer building a diverse and inclusive workforce. If you need additional accommodations to feel comfortable during your interview process, please email us at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accessibility@cockroachlabs.com&quot;&gt;accessibility@cockroachlabs.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
